          <div id='post_6' itemprop="comment" itemscope="itemscope" itemtype="http://schema.org/Comment" class='topic-body crawler-post'>
            <div class='crawler-post-meta'>
              <span class="creator" itemprop="author" itemscope="itemscope" itemtype="http://schema.org/Person">
                <a rel='nofollow' href='https://discuss.python.org/u/CAM-Gerlach'><span itemprop="name">CAM-Gerlach</span></a>
                  <meta itemprop='url' content='https://discuss.python.org/u/CAM-Gerlach'>
                (C.A.M. Gerlach)
              </span>



              <span class="crawler-post-infos">
                  <time itemprop="datePublished" datetime='2023-01-08T22:17:34Z' class='post-time'>
                    January 8, 2023, 10:17pm
                  </time>
                  <meta itemprop='dateModified' content='2023-01-08T22:17:34Z'>
              <span itemprop="position">6</span>
              </span>
            </div>
            <div class='post' itemprop="text">
              <p>On an editorial note, shouldn’t this be moved to <a class="hashtag" href="/c/peps/19">#<span>peps</span></a> with all the other PEP-related discussions and announcements (aside from <a class="hashtag" href="/c/packaging/14">#<span>packaging</span></a> , which has its own category and process?) per standard convention and the current PEP 1, etc. guidance? I went looking for this thread everywhere there but didn’t find it.</p>
            </div>

              <div itemprop="interactionStatistic" itemscope="itemscope" itemtype="http://schema.org/InteractionCounter">
